@startuml sm_002_directive_lifecycle
' ============================================================
' Title:     SM-002 Directive Lifecycle
' Source:    docs/spec/contracts/directive/lifecycle.yaml
'            docs/spec/contracts/directive/identity.yaml
'            docs/spec/contracts/directive/amendment.yaml
' C4:        api → directives_application → directives_repository → directives_store
'            compile via outbox → compilation_application (no direct app→app edge)
' Package:   directives_application / directives_domain
' Contract:  1.1.0
' ============================================================

title **SM-002 — Directive Lifecycle**\nC4: api → directives_application → directives_repository → directives_store\n<size:12><i>Draft · Active · Deprecated · Superseded · identity spawn</i></size>

!include ./common/sm_styles.puml

[*] --> Draft : <b>DirectiveCreated</b>\nactor: Regulatory Official\ncommand: directive.create\n[capability: directive.create]\n/ assignLineageId()\n/ executionIdEqualsLineage()\n/ authoredByActor()\nstory: US-CP-001

state "Draft" as Draft #B9770E : **entry** mutable drafting\n**allowed** modify · publish compile\n**forbidden** retire · fork · merge · split\n**identity** lineage_id + execution_id fixed
state "Active" as Active #2C6E49 : **entry** published & operational in CG-IR\n**allowed** modify · retire · supersede\n**allowed** fork · merge · split\n**forbidden** create (new root uses Draft)
state "Deprecated" as Deprecated #4A4A4A : **entry** retired / absorbed parent\n**allowed** restore only\n**forbidden** fork · merge · split · modify body\nCG-IR nodes marked deprecated
state "Superseded" as Superseded #4A4A4A : **entry** replaced by successor\n**allowed** read-only audit trail\n**forbidden** restore without successor governance\nmetadata.migration.superseded_by required

' ---------- Hierarchical composite: identity operations ----------
state "Identity Spawn" as IdentitySpawn #1B7A6E {
  ' Initial required (STM-026); deep targets Fork/Merge/Split override on entry
  [*] --> ForkChildren
  state "Fork Children\n(spawn)" as ForkChildren #1B7A6E : **entry** 2 new execution_ids\nshared lineage_id\nlineage.operation = fork\nparent → Deprecated\nchildren enter Draft
  state "Merge Result\n(spawn)" as MergeResult #1B7A6E : **entry** binary merge only (v8.2.x)\nlineage_id = MIN(parents) lex\nexecution_id = lineage_id + "-M" + SHA-256(...)[0:16]\nboth parents → Deprecated\nchild enters Draft
  state "Split Children\n(spawn)" as SplitChildren #1B7A6E : **entry** N new execution_ids\nshared lineage_id\nlineage.operation = split\nparent → Deprecated\nchildren enter Draft
}

' ---------- Internal revisions (STM-018 / STM-035: no re-entry) ----------
Draft : <b>DirectiveRevised</b>\nactor: Regulatory Official\ncommand: directive.modify (revision)\n[capability: directive.modify]\n/ recordRevision()\n/ idsUnchanged()\nstory: US-CP-003
Active : <b>DirectiveRevised</b>\nactor: Regulatory Official\ncommand: directive.modify (revision)\n[capability: directive.modify]\n[exclusiveWriteLockAndCompileSuccess]\n/ recordRevision()\n/ idsUnchanged()\nstory: US-CP-003

' ---------- Status transitions ----------
Draft --> Active : <b>DirectivePublished</b>\nactor: Regulatory Official + System\ncommand: directive.modify (publish)\n[capability: directive.modify]\n[hermeticCompileSuccess]\n/ publishCgIrSnapshot()\nstory: US-CP-001 / US-CP-003

Active --> Deprecated : <b>DirectiveRetired</b>\nactor: Regulatory Official\ncommand: directive.retire\n[capability: directive.retire]\n/ recordReason()\n/ markCgIrDeprecated()\nstory: US-DL-001
Active --> Superseded : <b>DirectiveSuperseded</b>\nactor: Regulatory Official\ncommand: directive.modify (supersede)\n[capability: directive.modify]\n[supersededByActiveOrDraftId]\n[successorCompileValidated]\n§2.2.4

Deprecated --> Draft : <b>DirectiveRestored</b>\nactor: Regulatory Official\ncommand: directive.restore\n[capability: directive.restore]\n/ copyTargetRevision()\n/ preserveLineageId()\n[must recompile to re-activate]\nstory: US-DL-001

' ---------- Enter identity spawn (target specific substate) ----------
Active --> ForkChildren : <b>DirectiveForked</b>\nactor: Regulatory Official\ncommand: directive.fork\n[capability: directive.fork]\n/ parentSideEffectDeprecated()\nstory: US-ID-001
Active --> MergeResult : <b>DirectiveMerged</b>\nactor: Regulatory Official\ncommand: directive.merge\n[capability: directive.merge]\n/ bothParentsSideEffectDeprecated()\nstory: US-ID-001
Active --> SplitChildren : <b>DirectiveSplit</b>\nactor: Regulatory Official\ncommand: directive.split\n[capability: directive.fork]\n[nArySplitSharesForkGate]\n/ parentSideEffectDeprecated()\nstory: US-ID-001

ForkChildren --> Draft : <b>DirectiveChildrenSpawned</b>\nactor: System\ncommand: materialize child rules\n/ newExecutionIdInstances()\n/ draftStatus()
MergeResult --> Draft : <b>DirectiveChildrenSpawned</b>\nactor: System\ncommand: materialize merge result\n/ newExecutionId()\n/ draftStatus()
SplitChildren --> Draft : <b>DirectiveChildrenSpawned</b>\nactor: System\ncommand: materialize child rules\n/ newExecutionIdInstances()\n/ draftStatus()

' Stable sink: Superseded has no outgoing business edges → Final (STM-024)
Superseded --> [*] : <b>Finalized</b>\nactor: System

footer SM-002 · Contract 1.1.0 · directives_application · Selma

@enduml
